# AGENTS.md (portable)

Every repo that agents work in should have a root `AGENTS.md`. Cursor and OpenCode both read it. Treat it as the handoff file when leaving Cursor Premium for OpenCode or a CLI.

## Required sections

```markdown
# AGENTS.md

## Commands
## Layout
## Conventions
## Gotchas
## Current work
## Learned preferences
## Learned workspace facts
```

## Update rules

- After discovering a real build/test command, gotcha, or layout fact, update `AGENTS.md` in the same change.
- Prefer short bullets (max ~12 per learned section). Deduplicate. No secrets, tokens, or personal data.
- Point `## Current work` at `ROADMAP.md` when it exists; otherwise name the active branch or open PR.
- Do not invent commands. Only write commands that were run successfully or found in the repo.
- Keep OpenCode-compatible plain Markdown. No Cursor-only frontmatter in this file.
